# Each loop compares its counter with the bound twice in the text (once on
# the way in, once at the bottom of the body) and nothing jumps back up. The
# counter is the byte offset (ivar, 2026-10-12) and lives in X (the loop
# rule of the peephole, same day): cpx, no cmp, no shift.
count 4 cpx\.w #480
in clear: absent jmp @
in sum: absent jmp @
in clear: absent asl a
in sum: absent asl a
in clear: absent cmp\.w
in clear: present inx\n\tinx\n\tcpx
